1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Verify chain fields seq/priorRecordDigest/supersedes are ALWAYS present on every v2 record type; at seq==1 both priorRecordDigest and supersedes carry JSON null (not omitted, not empty string); WHY: §0.4 nullability rule for chain-founding records\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts:2700 RedEvidenceData.records[] is widened to hold mixed v1 and v2 records in one array with the same on-disk file layout (schemaVersion-discriminated); no migration of existing v1 stores.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-002\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Widen RedEvidenceData to a mixed v1 and v2 records array without changing the stored file layout\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"A record with an unknown schemaVersion (e.g. proofstory.red_evidence.v3) is rejected at parse/load time with a diagnostic, not silently accepted into the array; WHY: forward-compatibility must fail closed\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Empty records array parses and round-trips as an empty array; WHY: boundary condition for stores with no evidence yet\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"A store containing only v2 records (zero v1) parses correctly; WHY: new stories may never have v1 records\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Read a store with v1-only records; round-trip write and re-read; all v1 records retain schemaVersion proofstory.red_evidence.v1 and their original shape; WHY: no migration means v1 stores are untouched\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Read a store with mixed v1 + v2 records; both schemaVersion discriminators parse correctly; v1 records are not widened or rewritten; WHY: the mixed array is the core data model change\",\"id\":\"CHK-002:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"In the SAME commit as the widening: guard redEvidenceRecordSatisfied (packages/main/src/core/proofstory.ts:931) so its record.observedFailure.trim() at :932 (reached via .some() at :947 and missingRedEvidence at :1196) is only applied to v1 records — a v2 record must not crash the LIVE enforce gate (devGateMode/reviewGateMode/doneGateMode all enforce in lattice.config.json). Prove the diagnostic output is BYTE-IDENTICAL to the pre-change run on a v1-only store (RED signal A).\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-003\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Make redEvidenceRecordSatisfied skip every non-v1 record and prove all three gate verdicts are unchanged\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"RED signal A attack: write a v2 quarantine record (no observedFailure field) into a real story red-evidence.json; run the real proofstory_gate_check → must NOT throw TypeError at record.observedFailure.trim(); WHY: this is the exact live crash path (proofstory.ts:932 via .some() at :947 from missingRedEvidence at :1196) that throws today and must be fixed\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Inject a record with schemaVersion proofstory.red_evidence.v2 but WITH an observedFailure field present (a malformed hybrid): the version discriminator governs the skip, not field presence; the record is still skipped by the v1 predicate; WHY: defense-in-depth against malformed records\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"A store with ONLY v2 records (no v1): missingRedEvidence fires (no v1 record satisfies the predicate); the diagnostic names the target as missing; WHY: v2-only stores have no satisfying v1 record and must report missing, not crash\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"A v1 record with empty-string observedFailure: gate still rejects (trim() yields empty → unsatisfied); WHY: the guard change must not alter any v1 evaluation path\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"RED signal A baseline: on a v1-only store, capture the FULL diagnostic output of redEvidenceRecordSatisfied/missingRedEvidence BEFORE the change; after the change, capture the same output on the SAME v1-only store; outputs are BYTE-IDENTICAL (diff returns 0); WHY: the v1-skip guard must be transparent to all v1 paths — devGateMode/reviewGateMode/doneGateMode all enforce\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"On a mixed v1+v2 store where the v1 record satisfies the gate: proofstory_gate_check does NOT throw; v2 records are silently skipped; the v1 verdict is correct; WHY: v2 records must be invisible to the v1 gate predicate\",\"id\":\"CHK-003:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence/chain.ts partitions records by (storyId, acceptanceTargetRef); head resolution implements BOTH §3.2 (lines 957-964) conjuncts; the three §3.3 (965-992) integrity checks run with FORK rejection as an INDEPENDENT store-corruption/concurrency detector whose reason id is DISTINCT from the prior-digest (check 2) rejection.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-004\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Resolve the chain head by both uniqueness conjuncts and enforce the three chain-integrity checks\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Fork attempt: two records both claim the same priorRecordDigest as their prior link; first admitted, second REJECTED by check 3 (fork rejection) with a reason id that is DISTINCT from check 2 prior-digest-mismatch; verify both reason ids exist and differ; WHY: RED signal C — fork rejection must be an independent detector from prior-digest link failure\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Seq gap: head.seq=1, append with seq=3 → rejected by check 1 with seq-gap diagnostic; WHY: gaps create uncheckable holes in the chain\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Seq reuse: head.seq=2, append with seq=2 → rejected by check 1 with seq-reuse diagnostic; WHY: reuse would create two records at the same position\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Prior-digest mismatch: append with priorRecordDigest that does not match head.recordDigest → rejected by check 2; verify this rejection reason id is DISTINCT from check 3 fork rejection; WHY: check 2 and check 3 detect different failure modes (broken link vs contested link) and must have independent diagnostics\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:adversarial:3\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Chain-founding record (seq=1, priorRecordDigest=null) on empty chain: all three checks pass — check 1 sees seq==1 on empty (correct), check 2 sees null==null (correct), check 3 has nothing to fork against; WHY: empty-chain boundary\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Two targets (AB-001, AB-002) in same store with same storyId: appending to AB-002 chain does NOT affect AB-001 head; head resolution is per-target; WHY: §3.2 distinct targets chains are independent\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Single-record chain (seq=1): resolveHead returns that record; verify conjunct (a) no other record references its priorRecordDigest AND conjunct (b) maximal seq; WHY: simplest chain, both conjuncts must hold simultaneously\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Three-record chain (seq 1,2,3): resolveHead returns seq=3 record; partitioning by (storyId, acceptanceTargetRef) isolates it from other targets; WHY: multi-record head resolution + partitioning correctness\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Integrity check 1 passes: newRecord.seq == head.seq + 1 (exactly, no gaps); check 2 passes: newRecord.priorRecordDigest == head.recordDigest; check 3 passes: no existing record claims the same priorRecordDigest; WHY: all three checks pass on a well-formed append\",\"id\":\"CHK-004:happy:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"The §3.3 closed transition table governs legal quarantine/recover transitions with governing-red-assert derivation; effective-head resolution walks transitively through chained recover records and is cycle-safe (a self-referential or looping recover chain TERMINATES instead of recursing forever).\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-005\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Implement the closed transition table with transitive cycle-safe effective-head resolution\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Self-referential recover chain: a recover record whose recoversRecordId = its own id → effective-head walk TERMINATES (does not recurse forever); WHY: cycle safety is a hard requirement, infinite recursion = crash\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Looping recover chain: record A recovers B, record B recovers A → effective-head walk detects the cycle and terminates; WHY: mutual reference creates a cycle that must be detected\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Recover-of-a-recover: current head is a recover record, attempt another recover targeting it → REJECTED by the §4.1 state machine (recover targets quarantine heads only); WHY: RED signal C — recover is only valid on a quarantine head\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Quarantine of a non-head record: attempt to quarantine a record that is NOT the current chain head → REJECTED; WHY: RED signal C — only the head can be quarantined\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:3\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Empty chain → green-confirm/quarantine/recover: all three REJECTED (empty chain admits only red-assert); WHY: no governing red-assert exists, so no transition is possible\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:adversarial:4\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"green-confirm head → red-assert (re-open/regression): legal; green-confirm head → green-confirm (re-confirmation of SAME governing red-assert at newer green tree): legal; WHY: these are the two less-obvious green-confirm successor transitions\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Transitive effective-head: chain has red-assert → quarantine → recover → quarantine → recover; effective head = red-assert (two levels of transitive walk); WHY: effective-head must walk ALL chained recovers, not just one level\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"green-confirm whose confirmsRecordId does NOT equal the current governing red-assert id → REJECTED regardless of chain ordering; WHY: a green-confirm must confirm the SAME governing assertion, not an old or foreign one\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:edge:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Empty chain → red-assert: legal; red-assert head → green-confirm (confirmsRecordId == governing red-assert id): legal; red-assert head → quarantine: legal; quarantine head → recover: legal; quarantine head → red-assert (deliberate replacement): legal; WHY: every row of the closed transition table accepts its legal successors\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Effective-head resolution for a recover record: recover reinstates the record retired by the referenced quarantine; effectiveHeadOperation = the reinstated record operation (transitively); governing red-assert derivation walks back through the chain; WHY: recover is transparent — it re-exposes the pre-quarantine state\",\"id\":\"CHK-005:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence/operation-key.ts derives the three §3.4 (1000-1050) operation-key preimages and normalizedReason, and the deterministic record id `<OP>-first12hex(operationKey)-<seq>`; first12hex reuses the W2a helper over the 64-hex body excluding the sha256: prefix.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-006\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Derive the three operation-key preimages and the deterministic record id from the digest body\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"approvedBy is deliberately EXCLUDED from quarantine/recover key: two calls with different sessionId (different approvedBy) but identical other fields produce the SAME operationKey; WHY: cross-session retry must dedupe correctly per §3.4 audit round 5\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"priorRecordDigest is NOT in any operation key: two calls with different priorRecordDigest but identical logical fields produce the SAME operationKey; WHY: §3.4 audit round 4 — retries after a successful append must not derive a new key\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Two calls with identical preimage fields but different non-key fields (createdAt, note) produce the SAME operationKey; verify the key is stable; WHY: non-key metadata must never influence deduplication\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:adversarial:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"normalizedReason: input reason with leading/trailing whitespace and internal multiple-space runs → normalizedReason trims and collapses to single spaces; two calls with cosmetically different whitespace produce the SAME operationKey; WHY: whitespace normalization is the dedupe-safety rule\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"first12hex extracts characters 7..18 (0-indexed) from the sha256:xxxx...xxx string, i.e., the first 12 hex characters AFTER the sha256: prefix; reuses the W2a canon helper; WHY: off-by-one in prefix stripping would silently fork ids\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Same logical operation at different seq values (e.g. retry after chain moved): operationKey is identical (seq is NOT in the key); recordId differs only in the trailing -seq suffix; WHY: §3.4 deliberately excludes chain placement from the key\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:edge:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"red-assert operationKey = CANON({operation, storyId, acceptanceTargetRef, baselineHeadHash, baselineMaterialHash, specDigest, assertionDigest, policyDigest}); recordId = RED-first12hex(operationKey)-seq; verify against hand-computed CANON; WHY: the 8-field preimage is the normative key derivation\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"green-confirm operationKey = CANON({operation, storyId, acceptanceTargetRef, greenHeadHash, greenMaterialHash, confirmsRecordDigest, confirmsAssertionDigest, specDigest}); recordId = GRN-first12hex(operationKey)-seq; WHY: green-confirm has its own 8-field preimage\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"quarantine/recover operationKey = CANON({operation, storyId, acceptanceTargetRef, recoversRecordId, referencedRecordDigest, normalizedReason}); recordId = QUA/REC-first12hex(operationKey)-seq; WHY: control key is the 6-field preimage\",\"id\":\"CHK-006:happy:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence/append.ts runs the mandated §3.5 ORDER: derive key → dedupe search → replay short-circuit (a replay deriving the same operationKey returns the EXISTING record, records.length UNCHANGED, no second run) → resolve head → transition legality → integrity checks → append; a stored record failing its own key/id recomputation raises a tagged CONFLICT with nothing written.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-007\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Order the append pipeline so the dedupe search precedes head resolution and any run\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Stored record with corrupted operationKey (recomputing CANON over the stored key fields does NOT equal the stored operationKey): tagged CONFLICT error returned, nothing written to the store, chain unchanged; WHY: RED signal C — store corruption surfacing at append time, not silently propagating\",\"id\":\"CHK-007:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Stored record