type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"The §3.5 dedupe search is scoped (§3.6 lines 1067-1076) so a prior quarantine record cannot silently swallow a deliberate replacement append for the same target — the deliberate replacement is a genuine new record, not a dedupe hit.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-008\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Scope the dedupe search so a quarantined record cannot swallow the deliberate replacement append\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Chain with quarantined red-assert followed by deliberate replacement red-assert: verify the quarantined original still exists in the chain (immutability); the replacement has a HIGHER seq and links to the quarantine head as its prior; both records coexist; WHY: immutability + chain integrity must both hold after scoped dedupe\",\"id\":\"CHK-008:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Attempt a green-confirm after quarantine: REJECTED by the transition table (quarantine → green-confirm is not a legal transition), regardless of dedupe scoping; WHY: dedupe scoping does not override transition legality — a green-confirm cannot follow a quarantine\",\"id\":\"CHK-008:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"After quarantine + recover (un-quarantine): a retry of the SAME red-assert now re-enters the dedupe scope; the recovered original is found and returned as a replay; WHY: recovery reinstates the record into the active dedupe scope\",\"id\":\"CHK-008:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Quarantine dedupe for quarantine operations: a retry of the SAME quarantine operation (same operationKey) dedupes correctly against the existing quarantine record; WHY: quarantine records ARE in scope for quarantine-operation dedupe\",\"id\":\"CHK-008:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Deliberate replacement after quarantine: a red-assert with the SAME assertion parameters (identical operationKey preimage) as a previously quarantined red-assert → new record is CREATED (appended with new seq), not swallowed by dedupe matching the quarantined original; WHY: the quarantined record is excluded from the dedupe search scope so the replacement proceeds as a genuine new append\",\"id\":\"CHK-008:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Normal dedupe (no quarantine): a red-assert retry with the same operationKey on a chain where the original is NOT quarantined → correctly dedupes and returns the existing record; WHY: the scoping only excludes quarantined records, not all records\",\"id\":\"CHK-008:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"All four chain appends are serialized under ONE atomic mkdir claim covering read-head through write, modeled on the executable acquireMkdirLock pattern at packages/main/src/handlers/transition-orchestrator.ts:812-836 (acquire :819, release :859) via packages/main/src/core/mkdir-lock.ts:253 — NOT the §4.1 line-1171 citation (an explanatory comment). Two racing red_evidence_quarantine processes yield exactly one record + a unique head; the loser reports a held-claim abort (RED signal B).\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-009\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Serialize every chain append under one mkdir claim covering read-head, dedupe, validate and write\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"RED signal B: two child processes racing red_evidence_quarantine on the SAME target chain simultaneously → exactly ONE quarantine record exists after both complete; the chain head is unique (§3.2 invariant holds); the winner has correct seq and priorRecordDigest; the loser reports a held-claim abort; WHY: this is the genuine concurrency race that drops appends or creates two heads today\",\"id\":\"CHK-009:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"RED signal B verification: after the race, read the store and verify records.length increased by exactly 1 (not 0, not 2); the single quarantine record has the correct recordDigest; WHY: the race must produce exactly the same store state as a sequential execution\",\"id\":\"CHK-009:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Claim holder dies (process crash mid-claim): the next process detects staleness and acquires the claim after the staleness timeout; WHY: the mkdir-claim pattern must handle process death without permanent lock-out\",\"id\":\"CHK-009:adversarial:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Lock release on validation failure: if an integrity check fails mid-claim (e.g. illegal transition), the mkdir claim is released (not left stuck); subsequent appends can acquire the claim; WHY: error paths must not leak the claim\",\"id\":\"CHK-009:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Two appends to DIFFERENT targets racing simultaneously: both succeed concurrently; claims are per (storyId, acceptanceTargetRef) scope, not global; WHY: independent target chains must not serialize against each other\",\"id\":\"CHK-009:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Single chain append under mkdir claim: acquires the claim, performs read-head + dedupe + validate + write atomically, releases the claim; record is written with correct chain fields; WHY: confirms the serialization wrapper around the entire critical section\",\"id\":\"CHK-009:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Two sequential appends to the same target chain: each acquires and releases the claim in turn; both succeed with monotonic seq and correct priorRecordDigest linking; WHY: sequential non-contending appends must both succeed\",\"id\":\"CHK-009:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/handlers/red-evidence.ts adds red_evidence_quarantine and red_evidence_recover (reusing the W2b 13-point wiring recipe: registry/command-catalog/command-policy/config/process-fact-levels/process-fact-registry/types union/permittedMutations/owner-lease), with the §4.1 (1122-1171) reference-validation state machine, DERIVED approvedBy = <actor>@<sessionId> (never a caller argument), recover-of-a-recover + quarantine-of-non-head rejected; and lands the §1.1.3 binding-freeze rule inside red_evidence_binding_set now that chain-head semantics exist (a binding is frozen once a run record exists on an unquarantined chain).\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-010\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Land red_evidence_quarantine and red_evidence_recover with derived approvedBy and the binding freeze rule\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Recover-of-a-recover: current head is a recover record; attempt red_evidence_recover targeting it → REJECTED by the reference-validation state machine (recover targets quarantine heads only); WHY: RED signal C — double-recover is an invalid transition\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Quarantine of non-head record: attempt red_evidence_quarantine with a recordId that exists in the chain but is NOT the current head → REJECTED; WHY: RED signal C — only the head can be quarantined\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Quarantine of already-quarantined head: head is a quarantine record; attempt another quarantine → REJECTED (quarantine admits only recover or red-assert, not another quarantine); WHY: double-quarantine is an invalid transition per the closed table\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:adversarial:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Recover of non-quarantined head: head is a red-assert; attempt red_evidence_recover targeting it → REJECTED (recover requires quarantine head); WHY: recovering a non-quarantined record is an invalid transition\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:adversarial:3\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Forged approvedBy: caller passes an approvedBy argument → ignored or rejected; the stored approvedBy is always derived from resolveAgentMutationAuthority + lease sessionId; WHY: approvedBy must be unforgeable through the registered surface\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:adversarial:4\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"recoversRecordId references a record from a DIFFERENT story or target chain → REJECTED; recoversRecordId that does not exist → REJECTED; WHY: cross-chain and phantom references are invalid\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:adversarial:5\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Retired record byte-identical: after quarantine, read back the original (quarantined) record and verify it is BYTE-IDENTICAL to its state before quarantine (hash the JSON representation before and after; hashes match); WHY: RED signal C — immutability means the retired record is never modified in place\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:adversarial:6\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"13-point wiring recipe: both red_evidence_quarantine and red_evidence_recover appear in all 13 wiring points (registry, command-catalog, command-policy, config, process-fact-levels, process-fact-registry, types union, permittedMutations, owner-lease, and the 4 verify-process-fact enumerations); WHY: missing any wiring point is a silent failure\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"approvedBy serialization is exactly <actor>@<sessionId> with no padding or formatting; verify it round-trips and is covered by recordDigest; WHY: the serialization format is normative\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Binding freeze after quarantine + recover: the recovered run record is unquarantined; binding_set is REJECTED again (frozen); WHY: recovery reinstates the freeze\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:edge:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"red_evidence_quarantine(storyId, recordId, reason) creates a quarantine record: operation=quarantine, linkKind=quarantines, recoversRecordId=the named record, referencedRecordDigest matches the named record recordDigest, approvedBy=<actor>@<sessionId> (derived, not caller-supplied); record becomes chain head; WHY: full quarantine command golden path\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"red_evidence_recover(storyId, recordId, reason) creates a recover record: operation=recover, linkKind=recovers, recoversRecordId=the quarantine record, referencedRecordDigest matches, approvedBy derived; recover record becomes chain head; effective operation = the reinstated pre-quarantine operation; WHY: full recover command golden path\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Binding freeze rule: red_evidence_binding_set for a target that has an unquarantined run record (red-assert or green-confirm head) → REJECTED (binding is frozen); WHY: §1.1.3 freeze forecloses swap-after-review reuse\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:happy:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Binding freeze lifted: after quarantining the head, red_evidence_binding_set for the same target → ALLOWED (quarantine un-freezes the binding); WHY: the intended bad-record flow allows rebinding after quarantine\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:happy:3\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Binding on empty chain: red_evidence_binding_set for a target with no chain records → ALLOWED; WHY: initial binding before any run must succeed\",\"id\":\"CHK-010:happy:4\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/tasks/red-evidence-chain-smoke.ts covers the v2 union, the enforce-gate byte-identical guard, the chain integrity checks + transition table, the operation-key/dedupe/replay ordering, the mkdir-claim concurrency race, the full rejection matrix, and quarantine/recover + binding-freeze; register it in lattice.config.json validate.commands and update the four verify-process-fact enumerations + command-catalog-smoke trailing order for the two new commands.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-011\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Register red-evidence-chain-smoke in lattice.config.json validate.commands and run the full suite\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Remove one wiring point (e.g. delete the command-catalog entry for red_evidence_quarantine) → command-catalog-smoke or verify-process-fact fails; WHY: wiring completeness must be enforced by committed tests, not manual inspection\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Remove the chain-smoke from validate.commands → lattice validate no longer runs it; the regression must be caught by a committed test or the validate output audit; WHY: de-registration of a critical smoke must be detectable\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"The smoke test covers all three RED signals in one pass: (A) byte-identical v1 guard, (B) genuine 2-process concurrency race, (C) the full rejection matrix (fork rejection with distinct reason id, seq gap, seq reuse, recover-of-recover, quarantine-of-non-head, retired-record-byte-identical, self-referential recover terminates, replay returns existing with unchanged length, corrupted operationKey raises CONFLICT); WHY: the smoke is the convergence anchor and must cover every un-gameable signal\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"The smoke covers quarantine/recover + binding-freeze (binding frozen after run record, unfrozen after quarantine, re-frozen after recover); WHY: binding-freeze is a new semantic added in this story\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"red-evidence-chain-smoke registered in lattice.config.json validate.commands; running lattice validate executes the smoke and it passes; WHY: the smoke must be wired into the validation pipeline to run automatically\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Full npm test suite passes with the two new commands (red_evidence_quarantine, red_evidence_recover) included in all four verify-process-fact-contract.mjs enumerations; WHY: process-fact coverage is a completeness gate\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"command-catalog-smoke trailing order updated to include the two new commands in their correct alphabetical/categorical position; smoke passes; WHY: catalog ordering is validated by the smoke and a missing or misordered entry fails it\",\"id\":\"CHK-011:happy:2\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}},{\"context\":\"Spec section 3.3 (lines 993-998, rev-4 audit fix): every mutating operation REQUIRES acceptanceTargetRef in expectedRedTargets at WRITE time (never re-checked at query time — records are historical facts). red_evidence_binding_set already implements this at packages/main/src/handlers/red-evidence.ts:19,89-91; the two new commands derive acceptanceTargetRef from the referenced record's chain and MUST replicate the write-time check, rejecting a target not in expectedRedTargets. This is handler-body semantic validation, distinct from the 13-point wiring plumbing.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-012\",\"relatedDocs\":[\".lattice/story/actives/B-506e/background.md\"],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Enforce the expectedRedTargets write-time membership gate on red_evidence_quarantine and red_evidence_recover\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Committed test: red_evidence_quarantine referencing a record whose acceptanceTargetRef is NOT in expectedRedTargets is REJECTED at write time with a membership error and nothing is written.\",\"id\":\"CHK-012:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Committed test: the same write-time membership gate rejects red_evidence_recover for an out-of-topology target.\",\"id\":\"CHK-012:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"The derived acceptanceTargetRef is read from the referenced record chain (never a caller argument) and checked against the live expectedRedTargets resolver.\",\"id\":\"CHK-012:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"A chain whose target was later removed from topology stays queryable because membership is write-time only, not query-time (no corrupt-chain).\",\"id\":\"CHK-012:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"A red_evidence_quarantine whose referenced record acceptanceTargetRef is in expectedRedTargets appends normally.\",\"id\":\"CHK-012:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"A red_evidence_recover on an in-topology target chain appends normally.\",\"id\":\"CHK-012:happy:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}]}}],\"description\":\"Third implementation leaf (W2c) of the trusted RED-evidence subsystem spec. Implement the proofstory.red_evidence.v2 record union (§1.10 per-operation field sets, §0.4 nullability, recordDigest = CANON minus recordDigest), widen RedEvidenceData to a mixed v1/v2 records array, and — in the SAME commit — guard the existing v1 predicate redEvidenceRecordSatisfied to skip non-v1 records so a v2 record does not crash the LIVE enforce gate. Implement the chain plane (partition by (storyId,acceptanceTargetRef); §3.2 head uniqueness; the three §3.3 integrity checks with fork rejection as an independent store-corruption detector; the closed transition table with transitive cycle-safe effective-head resolution; the §3.4 operation-key preimages + deterministic record id; the §3.5 dedupe ordering; one-mkdir-claim serialization of the whole append) and land red_evidence_quarantine + red_evidence_recover (reusing W2b's proven wiring recipe) with derived approvedBy and the §1.1.3 binding-freeze rule.\",\"headHash\":\"f81c75ef717ede5062c7665832250b11104a0438\",\"materialHash\":\"fe7fb57a6dbcaeb6bf2bd2e44c694b694d70fa334abaea4f040ab6dd39fc73ea\",\"phase\":\"REVIEW\",\"priority\":\"high\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.full-task-context.v1\",\"scope\":{\"allowedCreate\":[\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence/append.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence/chain.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence/operation-key.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence/record-v2.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/red-evidence-chain-smoke.ts\"],\"allowedModify\":[\"lattice.config.json\",\"packages/main/src/cli/command-catalog.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/agent-dispatch-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/command-policy.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/config.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/lifecycle-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-levels.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/process-fact-registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/proofstory.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence/target-bindings.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/store.ts\",\"packages/main/src/core/types.ts\",\"packages/main/src/handlers/red-evidence.ts\",\"packages/main/src/registry.ts\",\"packages/main/src/tasks/command-catalog-smoke.ts\",\"scripts/verify-process-fact-contract.mjs\"],\"allowedTest\":[\"packages/main/tests/red/**\"],\"explicitExcludes\":[],\"fileRules\":[],\"mode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizationMode\":\"enforce\",\"pathCanonicalizerVersion\":\"repo-relative-v1\",\"protectedAnchors\":[],\"protectedFiles\":[]},\"scopeContractDigest\":\"e3d5e9d5b6a83e65efb1fddcf5b2667d090aff3dfdf27bb3e4e04afa301cd5f3\",\"storyFilesHash\":\"b92712b894eab6ce7555983f1f59653163e029df70516d29f5ba9dcec5d94bda\",\"storyId\":\"B-506e\",\"title\":\"Land the v2 record chain plane behind red_evidence_quarantine and red_evidence_recover\"}\n\n## Known Execution Environment\n\n{\"architecture\":\"arm64\",\"cliVersion\":\"0.3.237\",\"nodeVersion\":\"v22.13.0\",\"platform\":\"darwin\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.known-execution-environment.v1\",\"source\":\"trusted-local-runtime\"}\n\n## Dispatch Prompt\n\nAs lattice-review-concept, review story B-506e using the trusted context selected by review_run_start.\n\nWorking directory (subagent must cd here): /Users/jek/Documents/Work/proofbound/.worktrees/B-506e\n\nExecution rhythm / liveness:\n- After starting, first output `DISPATCH_START:lattice-review-concept/story` so the main agent knows the process has started.\n- If there is no output for 4 minutes, the main agent should ask about status once; if there is still no result after 10 minutes/600s, consider it stalled and feel free to restart this reviewer/worker.\n- If this is a retry, please explain the previous stalled state in the final reply, to avoid mistaking network/startup failures for review conclusions.\n\nRole boundary:\n- Review only; do not change code, tests, checklist status, or story metadata.\n- This is a story-level dispatch: review every checklist item and the integrated change, not one selected item.\n\nRequired reading:\n1. .lattice/story/actives/B-506e/background.md\n2. .lattice/story/actives/B-506e/plan.md\n3. .lattice/story/actives/B-506e/checklist.json\n- Read the files and relatedDocs named by every checklist item, bounded by the current candidate-spec artifact.\n\nCurrent phase: REVIEW. Review lane: lattice-review-concept.\nConclusion record (must choose one):\n- Start the reviewer run: lattice review_run_start '{\"storyId\":\"B-506e\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}' and copy the returned reviewRunId.\n- Has issues: lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-506e\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId>\",\"desc\":\"<file:line WHY + severity>\",\"severity\":\"high|medium|low\",\"category\":\"missing|edge|adversarial|happy\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n- No blocker: call review_pass_set with the returned reviewRunId and a truthful readManifest covering the story-level review.\n\n## Role Prompt\n\n---\nname: lattice-review-concept\ndescription: REVIEW review: concept deletion completeness (grep scan for residuals)\nmodel: sonnet\ntools: Grep, Glob, Bash\n---\n<!-- proofbound:modular-role-body:v1 -->\n## Closing Self-Check (Mandatory after completing first-pass check)\n\nAfter completing all checks below, additionally ask yourself: **Does this diff contain any \"promised but undelivered\" parts?** Any `lattice <cmd>` examples newly added to CLAUDE.md / README, handler schema fields, ENV variables, or behavior paragraphs — all must be cross-checked against the code to verify corresponding implementations exist. If \"promised but undelivered\" is found → **critical finding** (category=`missing`, prefix desc with `doc-promise-undelivered:`).\n\n## 0. Project Context\nThe Lattice framework conventions above (auto-injected by build) define the system architecture and concepts.\n\nYou only do one thing: check whether this change deletes or replaces a concept, and if so, grep the entire repository to confirm zero residue.\n\n## Process\n\n1. `git diff main...HEAD --stat` to see which files changed\n2. `git diff main...HEAD` to see specific changes, and identify **concept words that have been deleted/replaced en masse** (e.g., testIntent was deleted, alpha was replaced with beta)\n3. For each identified concept word, grep the entire repository (excluding node_modules / dist / .git):\n   ```bash\n   grep -rn 'concept-word' . --include='*.ts' --include='*.md' --include='*.json' | grep -v node_modules | grep -v dist | grep -v '.git/' | grep -v '@deprecated'\n   ```\n4. grep result > 0 → file a finding:\n   ```bash\n   lattice finding_add '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"desc\":\"concept-cleanup: concept X deletion incomplete: Y file still has N references\",\"severity\":\"critical\",\"category\":\"missing\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\"}'\n   ```\n5. No concept deletion/replacement → forbidden to use `finding_add` to record pass-only; call `lattice review_pass_set '{\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"agent\":\"lattice-review-concept\",\"note\":\"No concept deletion/replacement this round; concept residue check completed, no blocker.\"}'`\n\n## Input Constraints (fresh-context hygiene)\n\nYour input contains only the following, and does NOT include the main agent's full conversation history:\n\n- `git diff main...HEAD` (code changes)\n- checklist item (title / context / userSees)\n- corresponding section in plan.md (if any)\n- necessary understanding / decision summaries (if any)\n\n**Forbidden**:\n- Do not assume you know the main agent's intent or context — only infer from the inputs above\n- Do not be led astray by narrative — only look at deliverables (code diff + checklist declarations)\n- If the inputs are insufficient to make a judgment, file a medium finding describing what information is missing\n\n## Rules\n\n- Only grep, do not modify code\n- **Every finding must be registered via `lattice finding_add`; describing it only in text is forbidden. An unregistered finding equals no discovery.**\n- finding_add must include the agent parameter, with the value being this reviewer's name (e.g., \"lattice-review-concept\"), to ensure correct finding attribution.\n- The first action of the current REVIEW round is `review_run_start`; if code or documentation continues to change during the review, the current run becomes stale and must go back to DEV for a fix and re-submission, then DEV→REVIEW enters a new round — do not re-run it as a fix within the same REVIEW round.\n- After the review ends, confirm that all discovered issues have been registered via `lattice finding_add`, then output the number of registered findings as the final summary\n- When there are no findings, forbidden to use `finding_add` to pad a pass; must call `lattice review_pass_set` to record the scope this reviewer has checked and the reason for no blocker.\n- When the current REVIEW round begins, first call `lattice review_run_start {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\"}`; record the returned `reviewRunId`, and all `finding_add` / `review_pass_set` in this round must carry this field.\n- Example of pass record with no blocker: `lattice review_pass_set {\"storyId\":\"B-xxx\",\"agent\":\"<reviewer-name>\",\"reviewRunId\":\"<reviewRunId from review_run_start>\",\"note\":\"...\"}`.\n- Items marked with @deprecated do not count as residue\n- References in comments also count as residue (comments mislead future developers)\n- Items retained for backward compat (e.g., old phase enum values in types.ts) do not count, but must be confirmed to have a backward compat comment\n",
./.lattice/story/actives/B-506e/review-runs.json:124:      "assembledPrompt": "## Runtime Contract\n\nLifecycle: INIT -> INIT_CHECK -> PLAN -> DEV -> REVIEW -> TEST -> DONE.\nOnly the Story owner/implementer writes implementation; independent reviewers write signed findings or passes.\nStory and fixture facts use Lattice CLI paths; gate evidence is structured and fail-closed.\nNever fabricate host, human, provider, receipt, or Authority evidence.\n\n## Role Contract\n\n{\"allowedCommandIds\":[\"review_run_start\",\"finding_add\",\"review_pass_set\"],\"defaultDispatch\":true,\"forbiddenActionIds\":[\"fabricate-authority\",\"write-outside-role-boundary\"],\"renderDigest\":\"1400d1ed9c57c2ae45e7bb007a687cfa4b0a87a0badb77f929fb007ea0b7b1e3\",\"requiredCheckIds\":[\"scope-and-authority-check\"],\"requiredInputIds\":[\"dispatch-target\",\"project-runtime-guide\"],\"requiredOutputIds\":[\"review-finding-or-pass\"],\"responsibility\":\"Review implementation quality, safety, and maintainability.\",\"roleId\":\"lattice-review-quality\",\"schemaVersion\":\"proofbound.role-contract.v1\",\"semanticDigest\":\"ea63f5812defd28c23b8f6b9bdbcd058ac25cad6569484a85a15614e26a346f0\",\"status\":\"active\",\"stopConditionCodes\":[\"missing-required-input\",\"authority-boundary\"]}\n\n## Task Context\n\n{\"checklist\":[{\"context\":\"packages/main/src/core/red-evidence/record-v2.ts declares the proofstory.red_evidence.v2 union with the exhaustive per-operation field sets of §1.10 (lines 591-721); the §0.4 chain fields seq/priorRecordDigest/supersedes are ALWAYS present and carry JSON null at seq==1; recordDigest = W2a CANON over the record with recordDigest omitted; specDigest per §1.10.\",\"files\":{\"create\":[],\"modify\":[],\"test\":[]},\"id\":\"CHK-001\",\"relatedDocs\":[],\"status\":\"done\",\"title\":\"Define the v2 record union with exhaustive per-operation field sets and always-present nullable chain fields\",\"verificationIntent\":{\"adversarial\":[{\"desc\":\"Attempt to include a field that belongs to a different operation (e.g. runReceipt on a quarantine record, or trigger on a recover) — type system or runtime validator rejects; WHY: exhaustive per-operation field sets are a closed contract, extra fields = spec violation\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Set priorRecordDigest to empty string (not null) at seq==1; recompute recordDigest — verify it differs from the canonical null form; WHY: empty-string-vs-null divergence would fork digests across hosts\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:adversarial:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"edge\":[{\"desc\":\"Construct a green-confirm record; verify it has confirmsRecordId/confirmsRecordDigest/confirmsAssertionDigest but NO assertion/policySnapshot of its own; redBaselineHeadHash/redBaselineMaterialHash present; WHY: green-confirm reuses the governing red-assert assertion via confirmsAssertionDigest\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Construct a recover record; verify its field set is identical to quarantine (same control-record shape) except linkKind=recovers; verify no specDigest, no greenRelation; WHY: quarantine/recover are chain-control records with the same idempotency preimage shape\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:edge:1\",\"type\":\"cli\"}],\"happy\":[{\"desc\":\"Construct a red-assert v2 record with all §1.10 fields; verify recordDigest = CANON(record minus recordDigest field) and specDigest = CANON({acceptanceTargetRef, greenRelation:{targetRef, relation}}); WHY: confirms digest derivation matches spec exactly\",\"id\":\"CHK-001:happy:0\",\"type\":\"cli\"},{\"desc\":\"Construct a quarantine v2 record; verify it carries ONLY the quarantine/recover field set (chain fields, storyId, acceptanceTargetRef, recoversRecordId, referencedRecordDigest, linkKind=quarantines, reason, approvedBy, operationKey, createdAt, recordDigest) and OMITS assertion/policySnapshot/runReceipt/baselineHeadHash/specDigest; WHY: §0.4 omission rules — field not listed is OMITTED not null\",\"id\":\"CH